# cuts/v1.0.58/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY v1.0.58: v1.0.57 WAS BUILT, INSTALLED AND WALKED, AND THE WALK FOUND A1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.57 is the first artefact in this sequence that reached a customer-shaped
# end state: cut, notarised, installed on a fresh macOS account, and walked.
# That walk earned its version -- it produced the A1 root cause, which no gate
# and no review had found across every prior cut.
#
# WHAT THE WALK FOUND, read verbatim off the installed box:
#
#     sys.path.append("/tmp/ostler-prelaunch-2026/lib")
#
# The store-auth .pth had the STAGING path frozen into it. That directory does
# not survive the install, so the import failed at EVERY python startup, for
# ever, on every install. Python prints "Remainder of file ignored", so the
# OSTLER_SECRETS_DIR default was never set and the auth wiring never happened
# -- cm059-editor 401s hourly and the Front Page never populates.
#
# 🔴 EVERY OBVIOUS CHECK PASSED ON THAT DEFECT. The .pth was present. The module
# was present and correctly installed at <final>/lib. Only the path INSIDE the
# .pth was wrong. This is why the fix ships with a BEHAVIOURAL test rather than
# a presence check: any test asserting "the .pth exists" passes on the defect.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT ADDS OVER v1.0.57 -- two fixes, both walk-derived
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   #595 / A1   store-auth .pth resolved OSTLER_DIR (the staging tree mid-
#               install) instead of OSTLER_FINAL_DIR. CM051 #1316.
#   #361        the installer sent an Apple Event to Finder, so macOS asked the
#               customer to let Ostler "control Finder" and reach "documents
#               and data" during an install that wants neither. CM051 #1315.
#
# ⚠️ #361 WAS FIXED BY DELETION, NOT BY COPY, and the reason matters. macOS
# permits exactly ONE NSAppleEventsUsageDescription per app and stamps it on
# every Apple Events prompt regardless of target, so no wording could have made
# that dialog honest while the Finder event still fired. v1.0.57 carried a
# pre-announcement (row A below) which softened the surprise; this cut removes
# the cause. `open -R` survives -- it is LaunchServices, not an Apple Event,
# and raises no TCC prompt.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE STAGING-FREEZE CLASS WAS SWEPT, WITH CONTROLS, BEFORE THIS PIN
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# #595 is the THIRD occurrence (#177, #578, this), so the class was enumerated
# rather than the instance patched. Predicate: a WRITE, executing ABOVE the
# OSTLER-PROMOTE-BOUNDARY contract line, whose CONTENT interpolates a variable
# tainted from OSTLER_DIR. At this pin: 8 flagged, 1 real (#595, fixed here);
# the other 7 are token/IP VALUES read via $(cat file) or `openssl rand`, and a
# token cannot freeze a directory.
#
# BOTH CONTROLS FIRED, so that near-zero is a measurement and not a vacuum:
# the same taint engine pointed at the real pre-#177 tree CONVICTS #177, and
# pointed at the fixed branch the .pth finding DISAPPEARS.
#
# 🟠 THE SWEEP ALSO NAMED WHY THIS KEEPS RECURRING, and it is not carelessness:
# tests/test_launchd_plist_no_tmp.sh discovers subjects by matching
# VAR="...LaunchAgents/*.plist". ONE artefact family. A .pth is not a plist, so
# it walked through a gate that was working correctly. Any NEW artefact family
# written above the boundary is ungated BY CONSTRUCTION. Widening that gate is
# tracked as #600 and is NOT in this cut.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DAEMON_COMMIT -- DELIBERATELY NOT ADVANCED. Do not "tidy" this line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# c6fc48c0 is hub-v0.4.69, the same daemon v1.0.54 through v1.0.57 named. THIS
# CUT REBUILDS NO DAEMON. Both fixes above are install.sh changes; advancing
# the daemon pin would claim a build that does not exist. Both halves of that
# release remain published (ostler-releases serves the daemon, ostler-assistant
# serves the hub app, BOTH fetched at the same DAEMON_RELEASE_TAG).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PIN IS TAKEN AFTER THE LAST MERGE, WHICH IS THE WHOLE LESSON OF v1.0.57
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gates-only dry run on v1.0.57's record REFUSED with "STALE PIN -- the pin
# does NOT name the install.sh being shipped", listing both merges above. It
# was right, and it cost nothing: a dispatch runs the checks and cannot reach
# the cutting job. CM051 below names origin/main AFTER #1315 and #1316 landed.
#
# NOTE THE GATE'S OWN WORDING, because it is the reusable part: "the pin IS an
# ancestor of the ref. That is not a defence. Ancestry proves ordering and says
# nothing about content." Ancestry is valid one way only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS CUT HAS NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT IT IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.58.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current target.
# The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote.
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE DMG IN THE WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in
# only $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop and $HOME of the account it walks as, and
# on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES artefact_sha256_source to read
# measured(...). A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere produces PROMOTE=0 for a
# reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than "wrong folder".

CUT_VERSION=1.0.58
DAEMON_COMMIT=c6fc48c0
CM051=0d104ebc8e5cffea3d30c9d9b99436a8d3884932
